Generally speaking I think you are refering to the PC-like
Alpha XL and XLT machines. These only have ARC/AlphaBIOS because
they were designed & mfgd by DEC's PC division. 

There is a second group of machines that have hacked-SROM
code that makes them unusable with VMS/Tru64. These are the
white-box variants of the fully-capable Alphas that can do
T64/VMS. These have SRM available.

The white ones are cheaper. And FreeBSD can run on both
white and full-blown (blue) boxes because FreeBSD understands
the SROM hack. See the source code for more info.

> pretty current, or there wouldn't be qestions about MILO
